## C3-C approved syntax
```text
pycircuit compile -c <one-source.py> --source-root <root>
  [--package-prefix <dotted-prefix>]
  [-I <interface-unit-dir>]... -o <unit-dir> [--replace]
```
```text
pycircuit link <unit-dir>... --top <qualified-module>
  [--parameters <bindings.json>] -o <program.ac> [--replace]
```

## pycircuit compile --help
usage: pycircuit compile [-h] -c SOURCE --source-root SOURCE_ROOT
                         [--package-prefix PACKAGE_PREFIX]
                         [-I INTERFACE_UNITS] -o OUTPUT [--replace]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -c, --source SOURCE   The one Python source file to compile
  --source-root SOURCE_ROOT
                        Capture confinement root for the source
  --package-prefix PACKAGE_PREFIX
                        Dotted source-unit package prefix (default: empty)
  -I, --interface-unit INTERFACE_UNITS
                        A published managed interface unit directory
                        (repeatable)
  -o, --output OUTPUT   Published source unit directory
  --replace             Republish the target under the same owner and artifact
                        kind

## pycircuit link --help
usage: pycircuit link [-h] --top TOP [--parameters PARAMETERS] -o OUTPUT
                      [--replace]
                      units [units ...]

positional arguments:
  units                 Published source unit directories: the complete
                        closure

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --top TOP             Qualified module of the source graph root
  --parameters PARAMETERS
                        Ordered JSON bindings for the root's static parameters
  -o, --output OUTPUT   Published program artifact path
  --replace             Republish the target under the same owner and
                        definition

## top-level driver
usage: pycircuit [-h] {compile,link,emit,build,sidecar} ...

positional arguments:
  {compile,link,emit,build,sidecar}
    compile             Compile one Python source into one published source
                        unit.
    link                Link an explicitly listed unit closure into one
                        published program.
    emit                Emit PYC MLIR (*.pyc) from a Python design file.
    build               Canonical flow: multi-.pyc emit + parallel pycc +
                        CMake/Verilator.
    sidecar             Inspect and verify sidecar schedule files.

options:
